    {
      "id": "b-115",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-107",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Primary Role: Additional Photography"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-108",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Director: Jonas Elmer"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-109",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Cinematography: Chris Seager, BSC"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-110",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Writers: Ken Rance, C. Jay Cox"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-111",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Stars: Renée Zellweger, Harry Connick Jr., Siobhan Fallon"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-112",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "URL: [https://player.vimeo.com/video/1059224986?h=45ff050604](https://player.vimeo.com/video/1059224986?h=45ff050604)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-113",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Project Description: [TODO]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-114",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Clip Description: NewInTownThis was Faires’ second film with Chris Seager, and it was a cold one. The coldest steadicam shot he has ever done (and hopes to ever do) was the walk and talk with Renée Zellweger and Siobhan Fallon. 57 below zero… Yikes! Having worked with Chris on The Merry Gentleman before this film allowed them to fall right back into that creative shorthand that is so valuable. Chris and Faires have very similar artistic aesthetics and they built a great trust and friendship for one another that he cherishes to this day."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-116",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Dan in Real Life"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-132",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-117",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Primary Role: 2nd-Unit"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-118",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Director: Peter Hedges"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-119",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Production Studio: Focus Features, Jon Shestack Productions"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-120",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "DP: Lawrence Sher"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-121",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Stars: Steve Carell, Juliette Binoche, Dane Cook"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-122",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "URL: [https://player.vimeo.com/video/1059224956?h=732e80fe76](https://player.vimeo.com/video/1059224956?h=732e80fe76)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-123",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Project Description: Dan in Real Life stars Steve Carell as advice columnist Dan Burns, an expert on relationships, but somehow struggling to succeed as a brother, qa son and a single parent to three precocious daughters. Things get even more complicated when Dan finds out that the woman he falls in love with is actually his brother’s new girlfriend. Carell is joined by a brilliant all-star supporting cast, including Juliette Binoche, Dane Cook, John Mahoney and Dianne Wiest."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-124",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Clip Description: This was an alternative ending that they had very little time to shoot. By the time they got outside the sun was where Lawrence Sher wanted it (right on the water) but they had hoped for a little more time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-125",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Primary Role: Additional Photography"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-126",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Creators: Eric Overmyer, David Simo"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-127",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Production Studio: HBO"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-128",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "URL: [https://player.vimeo.com/video/1059222042?h=da03703708](https://player.vimeo.com/video/1059222042?h=da03703708)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-129",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Cinematography: Lisa Rinzler"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-130",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Project Description: Treme is a television drama series created by David Simon and Eric Overmyer that premiered on April 11, 2010 on HBO. It takes its name from Tremé, a neighborhood of New Orleans. The series begins three months after Hurricane Katrina as the residents of New Orleans, including musicians, chefs, Mardi Gras Indians, and other New Orleanians try to rebuild their lives, their homes and their unique culture in the aftermath of the 2005 hurricane."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-131",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Clip Description: Faires was given the direction to “make it beautiful,” and don’t show the crane. Circumstances outside of the camera department’s control gave them one shot only… A daunting challenge to say the least! He’s still very proud of what they did in that one take. Obviously the studio felt the same and used this shot to end the film."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-133",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Faires learned his craft over the course of a twenty-year career, and has had the privilege of working with some of the most respected Producers, Directors and Directors of Photography. He also had the honor of being a member of an Academy Award winning camera department (\"JFK\"). Being a Camera Operator is a marriage between his athleticism (as an Olympic-trained sabre fencer) and a love of form and composition through Cinematography. With an attention to detail and a desire to challenge himself physically, he brings energy and artistry to every project."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}